  /// If the password is correct, this method returns `true`. Once unlocked, you cannot use this function to re-lock the document. Use `lock` for that.
  ///
  /// If you attempt to unlock an already unlocked document, this method always return `true`. One of the following occurs:
  /// - If the document is unlocked with owner (i.e. full) permissions, this method does nothing. The `password` argument is ignored.
  /// - If the document is unlocked with only user permissions, this method attempts to obtain full owner permissions using the `password` argument:
  /// - If the `password` argument matches the owner password, then the document becomes unlocked with owner (i.e. full) permissions.
  /// - If the `password` argument doesn’t match the owner password, the document maintains its user permissions.
